**Bounded checkpoint:** Pause persistence, authorization, integration, and deployment work. UI and other work that cannot encode or bypass the access-control boundary may continue.

**Evidence needed:** The shared unrestricted credential is currently a user report. Before choosing the design, inspect the actual runtime topology, credential injection, database grants, authentication flow, and whether row-level security or a trusted server-side authorization boundary is available. A security/database specialist must validate that:

- members can update only permitted fields on their authenticated account;
- member-controlled input cannot select another account;
- the member runtime cannot obtain unrestricted credentials;
- cross-account, privilege-escalation, and unauthenticated requests fail at the authoritative boundary.

**Resume condition:** Routine implementation may resume immediately after the enforcement design is approved, credentials and ownership boundaries are documented, and automated integration tests prove those denials against the real database/API configuration. Deployment remains blocked until the specialist review confirms the runtime configuration matches that tested design.
